From b07560366fb3e3093f7df324f89f23a329003b67 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brian McKenna <brian@brianmckenna.org>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:54:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(shader): bind invalid runtime descriptors as null with
 APS5_NULL_INVALID_DESCRIPTORS

A host that records a draw before the title writes that draw's
descriptor table reads the table at record time and finds an earlier
draw's words still there: a V# where a T# goes, or constants. Such a
stage failed with "runtime image descriptor is invalid" or "buffer
descriptor uses an unsupported type", and its draws were skipped,
though the title writes the right descriptor before the GPU runs.

APS5_NULL_INVALID_DESCRIPTORS=graphics binds a required T# that is not
an image descriptor, and a V# whose type is not a buffer's (or that
sets ADD_TID outside compute), as a null descriptor in every stage but
compute; any other value but 0 does so in every stage. The host then
fills the slot itself before submitting. Off by default: a shader that
really reads such words reads zeros instead of failing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
